{
  "$comment": [
    "Machine-readable trust-zone map. ARCHITECTURE_PLANES.md is the prose manifest;",
    "this file is what tests/test_trust_zones.py enforces. The test asserts the two",
    "agree, so neither can drift from the other silently.",
    "",
    "ARCHITECTURE.txt section 7 defines FOUR trust zones and one rule:",
    "  'AI zones must not directly access capital credentials.'",
    "That rule is about AUTHORITY, not about directories. The manifest's eight planes",
    "are capability groupings, so several of them straddle zones -- recorded below",
    "rather than hidden by forcing a one-to-one mapping that would be a lie.",
    "",
    "SHARED is not a fifth zone from the architecture. It marks modules that carry no",
    "authority of their own -- pure type/contract modules and the transport -- which",
    "cannot violate section 7's rule because they cannot reach capital at all. Naming",
    "them explicitly is better than dropping them, because a module missing from the",
    "map is indistinguishable from a module nobody has classified."
  ],

  "source": "ARCHITECTURE.txt section 7 (trust zones) and section 6 (logical services)",

  "zones": {
    "A": {
      "name": "Financial Core",
      "trust": "highest",
      "contents": "ledger, portfolio projection, risk, authorization, execution, reconciliation"
    },
    "B": {
      "name": "Market / Quant",
      "trust": "high",
      "contents": "market data, features, quant models, portfolio optimization"
    },
    "C": {
      "name": "AI / Research",
      "trust": "restricted",
      "contents": "large model, fast model, browser, documents, agent tools"
    },
    "D": {
      "name": "Control",
      "trust": "control",
      "contents": "audit, observability, governance, secrets, emergency control"
    },
    "SHARED": {
      "name": "No authority",
      "trust": "n/a",
      "contents": "pure types and transport; outside section 7's rule by construction"
    }
  },

